  "working": "Evaluate each statement:\n(A) Conjugate base of H₂PO₄⁻ is obtained by removing a proton: H₂PO₄⁻ → PO₄³⁻? Actually H₂PO₄⁻ loses H⁺ to give PO₄³⁻? H₂PO₄⁻ → PO₄³⁻ + H⁺? That would be PO₄³⁻ is conjugate base of HPO₄²⁻, not H₂PO₄⁻. So false.\n(B) AlCl₃ accepts electrons? Al³⁺ can accept electrons? Typically AlCl₃ is electron-deficient, acts as Lewis acid, not base. So false.\n(C) NH₃ can donate its lone pair, classic Lewis base. True.\n(D) Strong acid has weak conjugate base; e.g., HCl strong acid, Cl⁻ weak base. So false.\nThus only (C) correct.",
